  <section class="about-image container"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1499750310107-5fef28a66643?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=85" alt="A quiet desk with a notebook, coffee, and laptop" width="1400" height="720"></section>
  <section class="about-copy container-narrow"><span class="eyebrow">Why we are here</span><div><h2>Attention is worth protecting.</h2><p>Inkwell is an independent journal for readers who want more than the fastest take. We publish considered stories about design, technology, culture, and the everyday choices that shape a meaningful life.</p><p>We care about clear thinking, generous curiosity, and work made to last. No outrage cycles. No endless feed. Just a small collection of ideas worth your time.</p></div></section>
  <section class="principles"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow light">Our principles</span><div class="principle-grid"><div><span>01</span><h3>Stay curious</h3><p>Good questions carry us further than easy answers.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Choose depth</h3><p>We give ideas the space and attention they deserve.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Make it human</h3><p>Warmth, clarity, and respect belong in every story.</p></div></div></div></section>
